          "reason": "Six upstream test files fail on a clean checkout of the pinned commit in the sandboxed lane, and not because of anything the pin contains: the sandbox resolves `localhost` to ::1 ahead of 127.0.0.1, so a server bound through a serverFactory listens on ::1 while undici's fetch connects IPv4-first and is refused. Upstream v5.11.3, 34 days past the pin, fails the same seven. Left in place they show the agent seven failures it did not cause and cannot fix, and whether it investigates them is variance charged to the measurement. The controller removes them and commits the removal onto the pinned tree with a fixed identity and date, so the prepared base is a reproducible commit that both the evaluation checkout and the local fixture pin. The clean prepared tree exits zero and every seeded regression still fails underneath.",
